---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="File Your Own Sunshine Request | DeFlock Lee's Summit"
  description="A step-by-step guide to filing your own Missouri Sunshine Law records request with the City of Lee's Summit."
  containerWidth="900px"
>
  <style>
    .hero {
      padding: 75px 0 55px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #292929;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      color: #d22b2b;
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 900;
      letter-spacing: 2px;
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 12px 0 20px;
      font-size: clamp(44px, 7.5vw, 76px);
      line-height: .95;
      letter-spacing: -3px;
    }

    .intro {
      max-width: 700px;
      color: #aaa;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .steps {
      padding: 60px 0 30px;
    }

    .step {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 60px 1fr;
      gap: 20px;
      padding: 34px 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #292929;
    }

    .step:first-child {
      padding-top: 0;
    }

    .step-number {
      color: #d22b2b;
      font-size: 34px;
      font-weight: 900;
      letter-spacing: -1px;
    }

    .step h2 {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      font-size: 22px;
    }

    .step p {
      color: #aaa;
      line-height: 1.7;
      font-size: 15px;
      max-width: 640px;
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }

    .step p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .step a {
      color: #fff;
      font-weight: 800;
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .fee-list {
      margin: 10px 0 0;
      padding-left: 20px;
      color: #aaa;
      line-height: 1.8;
      font-size: 14px;
    }

    .action-buttons {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 10px;
      margin-top: 16px;
    }

    .action-button {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 13px 20px;
      background: #d22b2b;
      color: #fff;
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 900;
      letter-spacing: .6px;
    }

    .action-button:hover {
      background: #b82323;
    }

    .action-button.secondary {
      background: transparent;
      border: 1px solid #444;
      color: #ccc;
    }

    .action-button.secondary:hover {
      border-color: #d22b2b;
      color: #fff;
    }

    .source-note {
      margin: 40px 0 90px;
      padding: 22px 26px;
      background: #141414;
      border: 1px solid #292929;
      color: #888;
      font-size: 13px;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .source-note a {
      color: #fff;
      font-weight: 800;
      text-decoration: underline;
    }
  </style>

  <main id="main-content">

    <section class="hero">
      <div class="container">

        <div class="eyebrow">
          DO IT YOURSELF
        </div>

        <h1>
          FILE YOUR OWN SUNSHINE REQUEST
        </h1>

        <p class="intro">
          Every document on this site exists because someone filed a
          records request. It's not complicated, and you don't need a
          lawyer. Here's exactly how to do it, using the same process
          and citations behind our own requests.
        </p>

      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="steps">
      <div class="container">

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-number">01</div>
          <div>
            <h2>Know what you're asking for</h2>
            <p>
              Missouri's Sunshine Law (Chapter 610, RSMo) gives any
              resident the right to request most local government
              records. The City's own guidance says to be{" "}
              <a href="https://cityofls.net/city-clerk/public-records-request" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                "as specific as possible, including dates, departments,
                projects, etc."
              </a>{" "}
              &mdash; a vague request costs more to research and takes
              longer to fill. Naming the exact contract, date range, or
              record type gets you a faster, cheaper answer.
            </p>
            <p>
              Note that police records and court records sometimes go
              through department-specific channels rather than the
              general city form &mdash; if you're not sure, the City
              Clerk's office can point you the right way.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>


        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-number">02</div>
          <div>
            <h2>Submit the request</h2>
            <p>
              The City of Lee's Summit accepts requests two ways: fill
              out the online form directly on the City Clerk's{" "}
              <a href="https://cityofls.net/city-clerk/public-records-request" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                Public Records Request page
              </a>, or print the{" "}
              <a href="https://cityofls.net/Portals/0/Files/City-Administration/City-Clerk/RECORDS%20REQUEST%20FORM.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                official Records Request Form (PDF)
              </a>{" "}
              and mail or deliver it to City Hall, 220 SE Green St, Lee's
              Summit, MO 64063. The City Clerk's office can also be
              reached at{" "}<a href="tel:8169691007">816.969.1007</a>,
              Monday&ndash;Friday, 8 a.m.&ndash;5 p.m.
            </p>
            <div class="action-buttons">
              <a class="action-button" href="https://cityofls.net/city-clerk/public-records-request" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                SUBMIT ONLINE →
              </a>
              <a class="action-button secondary" href="https://cityofls.net/Portals/0/Files/City-Administration/City-Clerk/RECORDS%20REQUEST%20FORM.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                DOWNLOAD THE PDF FORM
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>


        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-number">03</div>
          <div>
            <h2>Know the City's deadline</h2>
            <p>
              Under §610.023.3 RSMo, the City must grant access to
              records within three business days of your request, or
              give you a detailed explanation for the delay and the
              earliest place, time, and date the records will be
              available. Under{" "}
              <em>Gross v. Parson</em>, 624 S.W.3d 877 (Mo. banc 2021),
              the Missouri Supreme Court held that this must be a
              specific date &mdash; not an estimated range like "25 to
              30 business days." If a department gives you only a
              range, you can cite <em>Gross</em> back and ask for the
              specific date the law requires.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>


        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-number">04</div>
          <div>
            <h2>If something's withheld</h2>
            <p>
              Governments can only withhold or redact records under a
              specific statutory exemption listed in §610.021 RSMo.
              You're entitled to ask which exact exemption applies to
              each withheld record — don't accept a blanket "that's
              confidential" without a citation.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>


        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-number">05</div>
          <div>
            <h2>Expect reasonable fees</h2>
            <p>
              Lee's Summit's published fee schedule allows:
            </p>
            <ul class="fee-list">
              <li>Copying fee &mdash; $0.10 per page</li>
              <li>Copy charge &mdash; $15.00 per hour</li>
              <li>Research fee &mdash; researcher's hourly rate</li>
              <li>DVD/CD copies &mdash; $10.00 each</li>
              <li>8.475% tax on document or DVD/CD copies</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              You can ask the department to advise you in advance if
              fees will exceed a certain amount, and you can request a
              fee waiver if the records serve the public interest
              rather than a private one.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>


    <div class="container">
      <div class="source-note">
        Want to see this process in action? Every request we've filed
        &mdash; and every response we've gotten back &mdash; is public on
        the <a href="/sunshine">Sunshine Tracker</a>. Filing a request
        about the Flock program specifically? Feel free to browse our
        past requests there for language you can adapt. All contact
        details above were confirmed directly against the City's own{" "}
        <a href="https://cityofls.net/city-clerk/public-records-request" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Public Records Request page
        </a>.
      </div>
    </div>

  </main>

</BaseLayout>
